think Rota lap 11 reads active-designing/yonder/20260618-182412_single-stranded.md -- simple and easy are different; build by composing free parts each about one thing, and refuse the braid. The doc's own teaching pointed straight at the shape of this lap.
think The prior lap seated group_of (hue family). The plain human way to name a color is TWO words -- "dark blue" -- a tone and a family. The single-stranded reading says: do not braid tone into group_of; make tone its OWN module about one thing (lightness), so a caller composes tone_of + group_of rather than one function holding both concerns.
think tone_of(c) reads color.rgb_to_hsl and looks at lightness ALONE, returning dark / mid / light against two named edges (tone_dark_max 34, tone_light_min 70). It ignores hue and saturation entirely -- the single concern it holds. mid is the neutral tone a description leaves unspoken ("blue", not "mid blue").
think Verified the lightness math before choosing edges: black l=0, white l=100, red/gray l=50, darkblue #00008b l~27, lightblue #add8e6 l~79, and the exact edge greys #585858 (l=35) and #575757 (l=34). Chose the bands so each test lands where I proved it would.
obs GREEN on the FIRST metal run, no reds. Proven: all three tones reachable; a deep shade reads dark and a pale tint light whatever the hue; tone follows lightness ALONE (a red and a gray of the same lightness read the same tone, so hue/saturation never sway it -- the single-stranded crux); the band edges land on the right side (l=35 mid, l=34 dark); tone_of always returns a member of the sorted three; deterministic.
obs Kept it a SEPARATE module from color_name_group deliberately, honoring single-stranded -- each about one thing, composed into "dark blue" not braided. This is the reward the doc names: either can be reasoned about and changed apart from the other.
obs tame_style_check bans clean, width-check exit 0, plain 7-bit ASCII, American spelling, >= 2 positive asserts per fn, no seam cast (u8 percent only). Witness native contains (REDS #76 loom). image/README.md names color_tone.rye beside color_name_group.rye (docs-sync).
